# HoloScript Mini — Complete Technical Analysis

---

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

### What This Project Does
**HoloScript Mini** is a **real-time, gesture-controlled holographic object renderer**. It uses your webcam to track your hand, recognizes specific gestures, and responds by manipulating a 3D object (currently a square) on screen — rotating it, zooming it, or freezing it — purely through hand movements, no mouse or keyboard required.

### Type of Application
- **Desktop application** (no web, no server, no database)
- **Multi-threaded**: Two parallel threads — one reads the camera and interprets gestures, the other draws the scene at 30 FPS
- **Computer Vision + Real-time Rendering pipeline**

### Technologies Used
| Technology | Role |
|---|---|
| **Python 3.7+** | Primary language |
| **OpenCV (`cv2`)** | Camera capture, frame drawing, window display |
| **MediaPipe Tasks Vision API** | AI-based hand landmark detection (21-point model) |
| **NumPy** | Matrix math for rotation, normalization, smoothing |
| **threading** | Separates gesture detection from rendering |
| **math** | Trigonometric rotation calculations |
| **collections.deque** | Ring buffers for logs and scene history |
| **pathlib.Path** | Cross-platform file path resolution |

