#### Threading Methods

**`start_thread()`** (Lines 609–621):
```python
self.thread = threading.Thread(target=self._camera_loop, daemon=True)
self.thread.start()
```
`daemon=True` means: if the main thread (renderer) exits, Python automatically kills this background thread without needing an explicit `stop()` call. (Though `stop()` is still called in `finally` for clean resource release.)

**`stop()`** (Lines 623–642):
```python
